WEBVTT

00:00.700 --> 00:03.385
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:03.922 --> 00:07.274
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:07.309 --> 00:10.945
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:10.979 --> 00:13.764
♪ On which we used to rely?

00:13.799 --> 00:17.368
♪ Lucky there's a family guy

00:17.419 --> 00:20.738
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.772 --> 00:22.306
♪ All the things that make us

00:22.341 --> 00:24.074
♪ Laugh and cry

00:24.108 --> 00:29.280
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:29.305 --> 00:33.304
<font color=#00FF00>♪ Family Guy 11x04 ♪</font>
<font color=#00FFFF>Yug Ylimaf</font>
Original Air Date on November 11, 2012

00:33.305 --> 00:38.306
== sync, corrected by <font color="#00ff00">elderman</font> ==

00:39.140 --> 00:40.157
Hi, there.

00:40.191 --> 00:42.158
Hi. I'm Cindy.

00:42.192 --> 00:43.461
The only way I
believe I'm pretty

00:43.462 --> 00:45.045
is if strangers
have sex with me.

00:45.079 --> 00:47.832
Well, maybe I could help fill
you up with self-confidence.

00:47.866 --> 00:49.099
Brian.

00:49.133 --> 00:50.116
Hello there, sexy.

00:50.151 --> 00:51.102
Hey, do you mind?

00:51.136 --> 00:52.370
We were having
a conversation.

00:52.404 --> 00:55.957
My house has 8,000 square feet,
zero bookshelves.

00:55.991 --> 00:58.375
Wow, that's impressive.

00:58.409 --> 01:00.261
I'm a writer,
published twice.

01:00.295 --> 01:01.978
I own a cinder block yard.

01:02.013 --> 01:04.231
Have over 12,000
cinder blocks.

01:04.266 --> 01:07.067
If you ever need cinder block,
I can get you good price.

01:07.101 --> 01:08.184
Thank you.

01:08.219 --> 01:10.920
I-I have a six-CD changer,
so you can pretty much

01:10.955 --> 01:13.307
fill the tray
and create a world.

01:13.342 --> 01:14.641
Come have sex with me.

01:14.675 --> 01:17.495
My mother will make you
farkshekoosh when we are done.

01:17.529 --> 01:19.829
Okay.

01:19.880 --> 01:21.298
Wait!

01:21.332 --> 01:23.616
I have a time machine.

01:23.651 --> 01:25.218
You do?

01:25.252 --> 01:26.287
Yeah, you want to see it?

01:26.321 --> 01:28.588
Yes, I want to see it!

01:28.622 --> 01:29.889
Better luck next time, pal.

01:29.924 --> 01:31.791
Some people got moves,
others don't.

01:31.809 --> 01:32.959
Been that way forever.

01:32.994 --> 01:33.943
You.

01:33.978 --> 01:36.212
Me. Sex.

01:36.247 --> 01:37.814
Him legend.

01:42.837 --> 01:45.188
Shh.

01:45.222 --> 01:48.575
Why do you keep a sleeping baby
in your time machine room?

01:48.609 --> 01:51.161
I-I don't know,
my decorator's terrible.

01:52.830 --> 01:54.814
(whooshing)

02:05.509 --> 02:06.760
Where are we?

02:06.794 --> 02:09.913
Ford's Theater,
April 14, 1865.

02:09.947 --> 02:11.865
Ooh, Valentine's Day.

02:11.899 --> 02:13.365
How romantic.

02:13.400 --> 02:16.336
Uh, yeah, sure,
you know me.

02:16.370 --> 02:17.536
(moaning)

02:17.570 --> 02:19.105
(gunshot)

02:19.140 --> 02:20.306
(all gasping)

02:20.308 --> 02:22.608
Oh, my God,
the president's been shot!

02:22.642 --> 02:24.687
If you ask me, the
president's the lucky one.

02:24.688 --> 02:25.197
How's that?

02:25.211 --> 02:27.731
He doesn't have to sit
through the rest of the show.

02:27.765 --> 02:29.032
(both laughing)

02:29.066 --> 02:30.366
(gunshot)

02:32.887 --> 02:34.887
(door creaks)

02:37.224 --> 02:38.807
