02:38.842 --> 02:40.894
Yes, I'd like
to return this printer.

02:43.246 --> 02:45.682
(whooshing)

02:45.716 --> 02:47.800
<i>HERBERT MORRISON: The frame is
crashing to the ground,</i>

02:47.834 --> 02:50.053
<i>not quite to the mooring mast!
Oh, the humanity!</i>

02:50.087 --> 02:51.687
<i>And all the passengers
screaming around here!</i>

02:51.721 --> 02:54.074
<i>And just when you thought
it couldn't get any worse,</i>

02:54.108 --> 02:56.308
<i>there's a dog having sex
with a woman!</i>

02:56.342 --> 02:58.761
<i>Oh, I know I said,
"Oh, the humanity!" before,</i>

02:58.795 --> 03:01.163
<i>but seriously, oh, the humanity
even more right now!</i>

03:01.197 --> 03:03.082
<i>I mean, come on!</i>

03:08.121 --> 03:10.873
So that's what restaurants
were like before desegregation.

03:10.907 --> 03:13.325
<i>It was quiet.
It was quiet.</i>

03:16.963 --> 03:18.847
Wow, Brian,
you've had quite a string

03:18.882 --> 03:20.916
of female guests
spend the night lately.

03:20.950 --> 03:22.818
Yeah, whatever you're doing,
it's working.

03:22.852 --> 03:24.920
<i>You should see the way
I have to pick up chicks.</i>

03:26.122 --> 03:27.256
Hi.

03:27.290 --> 03:29.324
(giggling)

03:32.594 --> 03:33.796
(whooshing)

03:33.830 --> 03:36.597
Well, I guess you can call
me the Man of La Muncha.

03:36.632 --> 03:37.883
(laughs)

03:37.917 --> 03:39.985
Hey, why does your
time machine have a sticker

03:40.019 --> 03:41.954
that says
"property of Stewie Griffin?"

03:41.988 --> 03:44.623
Uh, well, I-I...

03:44.656 --> 03:46.225
(sighs)

03:46.259 --> 03:47.693
All right, to be
completely honest,

03:47.727 --> 03:49.811
and because we've already
had sex, it's not mine.

03:49.845 --> 03:52.631
I use it all the time,
and the owner has no idea.

03:52.665 --> 03:54.298
In fact, he'd
kill me if he knew.

03:54.333 --> 03:56.418
Really? Won't he see that thing
on the control panel

03:56.453 --> 03:57.718
that says "years traveled"?

03:57.753 --> 03:59.254
What thing?

04:01.924 --> 04:04.359
Here's where Brian goes berserk.

04:04.394 --> 04:06.410
(yelling)

04:09.165 --> 04:11.632
(yelling continues)

04:15.821 --> 04:19.123
(yelling winds down)

04:19.141 --> 04:20.842
Look, it's no big deal.

04:20.893 --> 04:22.793
Just reverse it
and take off the miles.

04:22.828 --> 04:25.463
That's what I do
when I take my dad's car out.

04:25.482 --> 04:27.482
Are you... are you 16?

04:27.516 --> 04:29.217
I will be next September.

04:29.251 --> 04:30.652
Well, I think someone

04:30.686 --> 04:34.055
has a Barnes & Noble gift card
coming for their silence.

04:40.062 --> 04:41.696
(groaning)

04:41.730 --> 04:42.931
(grunts, glass breaks)

04:47.719 --> 04:49.604
(electrical hissing)

04:51.823 --> 04:53.574
(high-pitched chirping)

04:53.609 --> 04:55.193
(electrical hissing)

04:57.379 --> 04:59.597
Brian, what the hell
are you doing in here?

04:59.631 --> 05:01.048
What's happening
to my time machine?

05:01.099 --> 05:02.216
I-I don't know, man.

05:02.267 --> 05:03.935
I-I saw Meg leaving
a minute ago,

05:03.969 --> 05:05.453
going, "Wah-ha-ha-ha-ha,"
but I-I don't know.

05:05.487 --> 05:08.605
(loud, droning whirring)

05:10.859 --> 05:12.109
(whooshing,
electrical hissing)

05:12.144 --> 05:14.145
(explosive pop, whirring)

05:20.018 --> 05:22.370
Oh, my God, it's having
a complete meltdown!

05:24.156 --> 05:26.489
(electrical hissing, beeps)

05:26.523 --> 05:27.692
(loud whooshing)

05:27.726 --> 05:30.227
(yelling)

05:40.806 --> 05:42.205
What happened?

05:42.240 --> 05:43.640
I don't know.

05:43.674 --> 05:46.042
(steam hissing)

05:46.077 --> 05:48.629
Dear God, my
time machine!

05:50.581 --> 05:52.967
You, uh... you want
to tell me about this?

05:53.001 --> 05:54.968
See? I told you.
It was Meg.

05:55.002 --> 05:56.236
I don't think so.

05:56.270 --> 05:58.172
The crotch doesn't
look like a BMX track.

05:58.206 --> 06:00.140
You bastard! You've been
using my time machine

06:00.174 --> 06:01.408
to nail your
bar skanks!

06:01.442 --> 06:03.143
Oh, come on,
they're not all bad.

06:03.177 --> 06:05.345
Oh, yes, I've seen the
women you bring home.

06:05.379 --> 06:07.497
That stutterer?
She was a real prize.

06:07.531 --> 06:09.399
How are you enjoying
your meal?

06:09.433 --> 06:13.270
L-L-Lois, it's
d-d-d-delicious.

06:13.304 --> 06:14.922
Oh, for crying out loud.

06:14.957 --> 06:17.240
Peter, why are you turning up
the heat again?

06:17.258 --> 06:19.759
Lois, this woman
is obviously freezing.

06:19.794 --> 06:21.361
Brian, I want
you to tell me

06:21.395 --> 06:23.196
exactly what you did
to my time machine.

06:23.230 --> 06:26.049
Well, I didn't want you
to find out I'd been using it,

06:26.083 --> 06:28.952
so I tried turning the
chronological gauge backward.

06:28.986 --> 06:30.787
It's not designed to
go backward, Brian.

06:30.821 --> 06:33.690
The question is, how
am I going to fix it?

06:33.724 --> 06:36.092
What the hell?

06:46.404 --> 06:49.738
Dear God,
everything's moving backward.

06:49.773 --> 06:51.141
What? What are
you talking about?

06:51.175 --> 06:53.075
I don't know
what the hell you did

06:53.109 --> 06:54.544
with all your
messing around, Brian,

06:54.578 --> 06:55.779
but somehow my machine seems

06:55.813 --> 06:57.513
to have reversed
the direction of time.

06:57.547 --> 06:59.082
Reversed the
direction of time?

06:59.116 --> 07:00.583
Stewie, what does
that even mean?

07:00.617 --> 07:01.900
I don't get it.

07:06.439 --> 07:07.807
Oh, ok, now I get it.

07:19.516 --> 07:22.252
Stewie, you can't just change
the direction of time.

07:22.287 --> 07:23.383
H-How is this even possible?

07:23.384 --> 07:24.634
Well, clearly,
when you attempted

07:24.668 --> 07:26.552
to reverse the gauge
on my time machine,

07:26.587 --> 07:28.805
you somehow released a quantum
shock wave powerful enough

07:28.839 --> 07:31.224
to push the flow of time
in the opposite direction.

07:31.258 --> 07:34.511
I can only surmise that you and
I were isolated from its effects

07:34.545 --> 07:36.079
because we were inside
the machine

07:36.113 --> 07:37.563
at the moment
of temporal inversion.

07:37.598 --> 07:39.582
Are you...
are you sleeping?

07:39.616 --> 07:41.684
Huh? No, no, I...
No, I was listening.

07:41.719 --> 07:44.420
What kind of jerk alters time,
and then falls asleep?

07:44.455 --> 07:47.540
Look, I'm sorry, Stewie,
but do you think you can fix it?

07:47.574 --> 07:49.926
Well, it's gonna take a while
to rebuild the machine,

07:49.960 --> 07:52.111
and even longer to
recalibrate it for normal time,

07:52.146 --> 07:54.113
but I've taken on
bigger challenges before.

07:54.148 --> 07:57.750
I had to explain to America why
Heidi Klum broke up with Seal.

07:57.785 --> 08:00.019
Face.

08:01.455 --> 08:04.006
There, now you've got
a fresh new diaper, Stewie.

08:04.041 --> 08:05.658
What are you talking about?

08:05.692 --> 08:07.343
What's going on?

08:07.377 --> 08:10.413
I think you're getting
a diaper change.

08:10.447 --> 08:12.881
Aah! Get that poop-filled thing
away from me!

08:12.915 --> 08:15.935
No! Oh, God,
it's cold!

08:15.969 --> 08:19.188
Whew! Smells like somebody
needs a diaper change.

08:19.223 --> 08:20.389
Damn right I do!

08:20.424 --> 08:21.958
Now, get this turd-filled
sack off...

08:21.992 --> 08:24.527
Oh, my God,
it just went back in my body.

08:25.795 --> 08:27.730
Hey, look, what's
wrong with Peter?

08:27.765 --> 08:30.232
(snoring)

08:30.266 --> 08:32.635
Oh, you smell that?
He's passed out drunk.

08:32.669 --> 08:34.971
Does no one in this house
have any dignity?

08:35.005 --> 08:36.572
(whooshing)

08:36.607 --> 08:39.342
Hey, Lois, I'm home from
the Clam, and I'm horny.

08:49.753 --> 08:52.355
(tires squealing)

08:54.524 --> 08:57.210
(tires squealing)

08:57.244 --> 08:59.945
Hmm. Seems like reverse
time did that kid a favor.

08:59.979 --> 09:01.747
I'm not so sure about that.

09:03.065 --> 09:05.968
Stand up! You're gonna
break that thermometer!

09:12.592 --> 09:14.610
My God, it's...
it's extraordinary.

09:14.645 --> 09:16.011
They all seem to be

09:16.045 --> 09:18.781
