11:54.551 --> 11:56.553
Damn it, I hate
these new stairs!

11:56.588 --> 11:58.571
(screaming)

11:58.605 --> 12:01.241
(bleep, bleep, bleep, bleep)

12:01.276 --> 12:02.476
(thumping, bleep)

12:02.510 --> 12:04.193
What are you watching?

12:04.228 --> 12:05.863
<i>Meet the Press;
it's really weird.</i>

12:05.897 --> 12:08.698
In reverse time, the Republicans
make outrageous statements

12:08.732 --> 12:11.434
and then the host asks
an unrelated question.

12:11.502 --> 12:13.303
Global warming is a myth.

12:13.337 --> 12:16.506
God created everything, and
the world is getting colder!

12:16.540 --> 12:19.076
What is your tax plan?

12:19.110 --> 12:20.209
That's odd.

12:20.244 --> 12:21.311
What?

12:22.580 --> 12:26.532
Man, we got a large number
of clovers on our lawn.

12:26.567 --> 12:30.336
No, no, no, no, no, no!

12:30.354 --> 12:32.155
Oh, hey, Cleveland.

12:35.610 --> 12:38.044
Australia, here I come.

12:38.078 --> 12:39.345
Look at that, Brian.

12:39.380 --> 12:41.364
Cleveland is back living
across the street.

12:41.398 --> 12:43.333
Cleveland left Quahog
quite some time ago,

12:43.367 --> 12:45.735
yet we only just recently
entered reverse time.

12:45.769 --> 12:47.220
So what does that mean?

12:47.254 --> 12:50.223
Well, it suggests that time may
not simply be flowing backwards;

12:50.257 --> 12:52.141
it may, in fact,
be accelerating.

12:52.176 --> 12:53.943
Accelerating?
Why would that be happening?

12:53.977 --> 12:55.078
I'm not sure.

12:55.112 --> 12:56.346
Have you ever heard
of a phenomenon

12:56.380 --> 12:57.914
called time dilation, Brian?

12:57.948 --> 12:58.981
Sure.
No, you haven't.

12:59.016 --> 13:00.750
Time dilation,
in forward time,

13:00.784 --> 13:02.652
is a phenomenon caused
by a variety of factors

13:02.686 --> 13:04.887
in which time
moves more slowly.

13:04.922 --> 13:06.856
In reverse time,
it stands to reason

13:06.890 --> 13:09.225
that the same phenomenon would
cause time to accelerate.

13:09.259 --> 13:11.327
I'll have to consult
my quantum calculations

13:11.362 --> 13:13.830
to try to isolate the
factors responsible.

13:18.001 --> 13:19.252
What the hell was that?

13:19.286 --> 13:21.154
This is more intense
than when I fought a rabbit

13:21.188 --> 13:22.587
in that karate tournament.

13:22.622 --> 13:24.424
That's weird. You're doing
reverse cutaways now?

13:24.458 --> 13:26.508
What the hell is... (screams)
What? What's the matter?

13:30.531 --> 13:32.865
Dear God, I'm un-teething.

13:32.900 --> 13:35.083
Brian, it appears the
flow of reverse time

13:35.118 --> 13:36.753
is beginning to
affect us as well.

13:36.787 --> 13:38.287
What does that mean?

13:38.322 --> 13:40.655
It means I'm going to have
to relive everything.

13:40.690 --> 13:42.725
Every painful,
awkward moment.

13:42.760 --> 13:44.793
Like that time I forgot
what came after "G"

13:44.827 --> 13:46.162
and had to fake it.

13:46.196 --> 13:49.698
♪ A, B, C, D, E, F, G...

13:49.732 --> 13:53.201
♪ H, I, J, K, L, M, N, O, P
♪ Ah-blah, blah-blah, blah-nah-wah ♪

13:53.236 --> 13:57.139
♪ Q, R, S, T, U, V
♪ Standing here with these kids ♪

13:57.173 --> 14:01.076
♪ W, X, Y and Z
♪ Waiting for the song to end ♪

14:01.110 --> 14:04.446
♪ Now I know my A-B-Cs
♪ Yankee Doodle went to town

14:04.480 --> 14:08.750
♪ Next time won't you sing with me? ♪
♪ Now I know my A-B-Cs.

14:08.785 --> 14:10.919
(crying, groaning)

14:10.953 --> 14:12.021
What the devil is that?

14:12.055 --> 14:13.188
It's Peter and Chris.

14:13.222 --> 14:14.956
Sounds like they're
in trouble.

14:14.991 --> 14:18.527
(groaning)

14:18.561 --> 14:20.696
My God, why is there
vomit everywhere?

14:20.731 --> 14:22.247
Is that the Ipecac bottle?

14:22.281 --> 14:23.482
Oh, no.

14:23.516 --> 14:24.683
No, please, not this.

14:24.717 --> 14:26.751
Oh, God, it's not gonna be
coming out of us;

14:26.786 --> 14:28.303
it's gonna be going...
(vomit noise)

14:28.337 --> 14:30.472
Oh, dear God...

14:30.506 --> 14:31.990
(groaning)

14:32.024 --> 14:34.009
Aah! What the hell?

14:35.445 --> 14:38.113
I don't wanna!
I don't wanna!

14:38.147 --> 14:40.165
Dad, I'm scared.

14:41.434 --> 14:43.752
(crying)

14:43.786 --> 14:45.454
Oh, God, this is so disgusting.

14:45.488 --> 14:48.039
I think I'm gonna puke.

14:48.074 --> 14:49.791
(bleep)

14:49.859 --> 14:51.877
(coughing)

14:54.713 --> 14:56.748
Stewie, I don't care
what it takes.

14:56.782 --> 14:58.849
We have got to fix this.

14:58.884 --> 15:01.453
We just ate so much vomit.

15:01.487 --> 15:03.687
Brian, it gets worse.

15:03.722 --> 15:07.791
Look.

15:07.826 --> 15:09.794
Yeah, Bonnie's pregnant
with Susie. So?

15:09.829 --> 15:12.062
That means Susie's
been un-born.

15:12.097 --> 15:13.698
Oh, my God.

15:13.733 --> 15:15.616
Stewie, you're not
that much older than Susie.

15:15.650 --> 15:17.619
Brian, if we don't find a way

15:17.653 --> 15:19.287
to push time forward again soon,

15:19.322 --> 15:22.707
I, too, shall be un-born.

15:27.713 --> 15:29.997
♪ You've got

15:30.031 --> 15:35.820
♪ The AIDS.

15:35.855 --> 15:37.821
That guy's gonna feel
so much better

15:37.856 --> 15:39.858
after we do what we got planned.

15:46.444 --> 15:48.879
How much time do we have
before you're un-born?

15:48.913 --> 15:51.198
With the time acceleration,
I'm not quite sure.

15:51.232 --> 15:53.633
But trust me, I can feel
myself getting younger.

15:53.668 --> 15:55.318
All right.

15:55.353 --> 15:56.603
The machine has
been repaired.

15:56.654 --> 15:58.688
Now all I've got to do
is isolate the cause

15:58.723 --> 15:59.789
of the acceleration curve

15:59.824 --> 16:01.858
and see if I can
duplicate the shock wave.

16:01.893 --> 16:03.076
(screams)

16:03.110 --> 16:04.261
What's the matter?

16:04.295 --> 16:06.863
I've regressed to my
pre-ambulatory stage.

16:06.898 --> 16:08.582
I can no longer walk!

16:08.616 --> 16:10.900
(grunting)

16:10.918 --> 16:13.236
My God, Stew,
you look terrible.

16:13.271 --> 16:15.005
Brian, I suddenly feel as if

16:15.039 --> 16:18.073
I've just been through
some sort of major trauma.

16:18.108 --> 16:21.177
Uh-oh. I think I know
what that major trauma was.

16:21.212 --> 16:23.146
(gasps)
My birth.

16:23.180 --> 16:24.981
Dear God, I've got
to get out of here!

16:26.317 --> 16:28.051
(gasps)

16:31.404 --> 16:32.873
Oh, he's so cute.

16:32.907 --> 16:34.874
Oh, my God, we're getting
closer to the beginning.

16:34.908 --> 16:36.576
You're Lacey Chabert.

16:36.611 --> 16:38.111
Oh, boy, a baby.

16:38.145 --> 16:40.981
I saw my Spanish teacher
leave one of you in a trash can.

16:41.015 --> 16:42.449
Brian, help!

16:42.483 --> 16:44.049
Stewie, what do I do?

16:44.084 --> 16:46.469
He's gorgeous, isn't he?

16:46.504 --> 16:48.520
I want to be the baby!

16:48.555 --> 16:50.023
Look at that head.

16:50.057 --> 16:51.724
Well, Lois,
this kind of completes

16:51.758 --> 16:53.693
your little carnival here.

16:53.728 --> 16:54.828
Hey, little guy.

16:54.862 --> 16:56.695
You ever need white,
corner-of-the-mouth stuff,

16:56.730 --> 16:58.882
you come to your grandpa.

16:58.916 --> 17:02.017
Stewie, this is
your new home.

17:02.019 --> 17:03.470
Brian, help!
It's up to you.

17:03.504 --> 17:06.121
You've got to restore
the flow of time.

17:06.139 --> 17:08.624
My life depends on it!

17:09.926 --> 17:12.128
What? Stewie, I don't know
how to fix that machine.

17:12.146 --> 17:13.479
Trust me, you can do it.

17:13.513 --> 17:15.599
You're so talented
in so many ways.

17:15.633 --> 17:16.600
Like what?

17:16.634 --> 17:18.100
Like... You...

17:18.134 --> 17:19.768
Just write down however
you think you're talented,

17:19.802 --> 17:21.537
and I'll sign it.

17:23.690 --> 17:25.057
Well, it's up to you, buddy.

17:25.091 --> 17:27.226
Save this marriage.

17:32.933 --> 17:35.968
Oh, my God,
it's the greased-up deaf guy

17:36.002 --> 17:38.570
running backwards toward
that grease truck explosion.

17:38.605 --> 17:40.673
Oh, the grease burns so bad!

17:40.707 --> 17:42.408
I can't hear!

17:44.177 --> 17:46.395
(in deeper voice):
Boy, I am late for that meeting.

17:50.116 --> 17:52.885
Come on, math, you dick.

17:56.556 --> 17:58.556
Come on, Brian.

18:04.147 --> 18:05.514
(machine whirring)

18:05.548 --> 18:06.548
All right, think, think.

18:06.583 --> 18:08.450
What do I do? What do I do?

18:08.485 --> 18:10.619
All right, could it be
as simple as this?

18:10.654 --> 18:12.036
"Invert time flow."

18:12.973 --> 18:14.707
Ah-ah-ah.

18:14.741 --> 18:15.890
Ah-ah-ah.

18:15.924 --> 18:17.242
Ah-ah-ah.

18:17.277 --> 18:20.912
Oh, he's perfect.

18:20.963 --> 18:23.931
Time of birth: 11:34 a.m.

18:23.966 --> 18:25.567
Come on, Brian, hurry.

18:25.602 --> 18:27.069
(cheering)

18:27.103 --> 18:28.503
It's a girl!

18:28.537 --> 18:30.289
With a penis and no vagina.

18:32.207 --> 18:35.911
No...!

18:35.945 --> 18:37.512
I think I can hear the ocean.

18:37.546 --> 18:39.181
Smell it, too.

18:39.215 --> 18:40.515
All right, what do I do?

18:40.549 --> 18:42.767
Wait a minute,
what did I do before?

18:42.818 --> 18:44.286
That's all I have to do, right,

18:44.320 --> 18:47.205
is duplicate the circumstances,
but do it the opposite way.

18:47.239 --> 18:49.023
All right,
I was standing right here,

18:49.058 --> 18:52.261
the machine was on,
I broke the glass...

18:52.295 --> 18:54.429
and I turned the gauge backward.

18:54.463 --> 18:56.932
Maybe if I turn it
in the other direction.

18:58.867 --> 19:01.170
(electrical buzzing)

19:21.490 --> 19:23.408
Ooh, a quarter.

19:23.442 --> 19:25.810
Who cares what that doctor found
on my nuts?

19:25.861 --> 19:27.895
This is a good day.

19:27.930 --> 19:29.063
It worked.

19:29.098 --> 19:30.831
I don't believe it. It worked.

19:35.721 --> 19:37.221
Brian, there you are.

19:37.256 --> 19:38.456
Where have you been?

19:38.490 --> 19:39.756
Meg, where's Stewie?

19:39.791 --> 19:41.492
Stewie? Who's Stewie?

19:41.527 --> 19:42.960
Here it comes.
Push, Mrs. Griffin.

19:42.995 --> 19:44.295
(groaning)

19:44.329 --> 19:45.780
You know what?

19:45.814 --> 19:48.582
I take it back, those panties
are gonna be in the way.

19:48.617 --> 19:50.351
Okay, here comes the baby.

19:50.385 --> 19:51.718
(groaning)

19:51.753 --> 19:53.521
Bloody hell!

19:53.555 --> 19:54.689
It's a boy.

19:54.723 --> 19:56.907
(cheering)
Oh, thank God.

19:56.941 --> 19:59.410
Oh, he's so beautiful.

19:59.445 --> 20:01.528
Mrs. Griffin, your husband's
standing right here.

20:01.562 --> 20:03.831
What should we name him?

20:03.866 --> 20:06.651
I kind of like
Brian's name: Stewie.

20:06.685 --> 20:08.652
That's a wonderful name, Brian.

20:08.686 --> 20:09.886
Stewie.

20:09.921 --> 20:11.839
Hi, Stewie.

20:11.874 --> 20:13.356
You did it, Brian.
I've got to say,

20:13.391 --> 20:15.576
I didn't think you were
gonna be able to pull it off,

20:15.611 --> 20:16.860
but you did it.

20:16.911 --> 20:18.945
You saved my life.

20:18.979 --> 20:21.782
And for that,
I shall be forever grateful.

20:21.816 --> 20:25.085
Hey, I couldn't imagine life
without you, buddy.

20:25.119 --> 20:28.256
You know, I forgot what a
man cave I had in Lois's uterus.

20:28.290 --> 20:30.340
While I was waiting for
you, I was shooting pool.

20:30.374 --> 20:33.443
Had to hold the cue at
weird angles, but still.

20:37.165 --> 20:39.916
Oh, Peter, isn't he amazing?

20:39.951 --> 20:42.986
Is he smart, or is he...
like me?

20:43.020 --> 20:45.021
He's perfect.

20:45.056 --> 20:50.057
== sync, corrected by <font color="#00ff00">elderman</font> ==

20:53.314 --> 20:54.831
<i>CHRIS:
You guys heard the baby</i>

20:54.866 --> 20:56.366
<i>talking in there, didn't you?</i>

20:56.400 --> 20:57.968
<i>LOIS:
Chris, that's ridiculous.</i>

20:57.969 --> 21:58.969
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru